<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>MCP caller-path verification (option C)</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 020, 021, 023 and 024; must finish before 025</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Task tags include auth and integration-test, and the task adds files under tests/** (root CLAUDE.md §8): code-review and adr-check run regardless</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security/auth-sensitive (tag auth): these tests are the evidence that every MCP tool runs as the caller over the unchanged IHttpContextAccessor path, which option C (FR-10) relies on instead of ICallerContext</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds only test files under tests/integration/{auth,data-mutation}/Mcp/ and test-only fixtures under tests/; shares no file with 031 or 040</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020, 021, 023, 024</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, testing, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Prove on a real host that MCP tool handlers on /mcp/legal-operations run inside the ASP.NET request, so the unchanged DataverseUserClient, CallerWhoAmIMemo and decision services serve MCP callers exactly as they serve REST. Write six tests: (1) the tool sees the request HttpContext and RequestServices; (2) WhoAmI over the MCP route, failing closed with UserContextRequired when there is no bearer token or no context; (3) one WhoAmI per MCP commit; (4) a plan-read stamp written over MCP satisfies an MCP commit; (5) a pin on the stateless transport with PerSessionExecutionContext=false; (6) every existing caller suite unchanged. Change no production code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core request scoping, IHttpContextAccessor and ExecutionContext flow, OBO token flows and WebApplicationFactory integration tests.</role>
  <goal>Six caller-path tests pass on the real MCP host, existing caller suites pass unedited, nothing under src/ changes, and unified-access-control-r2 plus two adversarial-reviewer passes accept the evidence.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07 (owner option C; notes/decisions.md 2026-11-07), which supersedes design §8 B-4. ICallerContext is deferred. MCP tools read the request HttpContext from IHttpContextAccessor; a null context or unauthenticated caller returns an isError result with UserContextRequired. Otherwise the tools call the same decision services REST calls: SignalReadService.ReadAsync(set, httpContext.User, ct); the DecisionPlanEndpoints body (SignalCoreRecordAccess, DecisionPlanService.GetAsync, DecisionPlanReadStamp.StampAsync(http), DecisionParameterSources.OptionsAsync(http)); and DecisionCommitService.CommitAsync(…, http, ct). Evidence for the decision: in ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1, StreamableHttpHandler passes context.RequestServices with ScopeRequests=false, and the default PerSessionExecutionContext=false keeps IHttpContextAccessor working inside tools. This task turns that evidence into tests. v1 limitation: decision capabilities run only inside an HTTP request. unified-access-control-r2 reviews this diff (project CLAUDE.md §4).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/McpCallerPathTests.cs (tests 1, 2 and 5)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Mcp/McpCommitCallerPathTests.cs (tests 3 and 4)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpTestHost.cs (from 020: the in-process MCP host)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Auth/ConfidentialClientMigrationSeamTests.cs (real DataverseUserClient behind a hand-written fake wire handler; copy the pattern, not the path)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/DecisionCommitServiceTests.CallerIdentityCount.cs (T170: WhoAmIs == 1 and every rights question asked)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/Signals/CallerWhoAmIMemoIsolationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/Handlers/Dataverse*HandlerTests.cs (chat dataverse.* handlers; must stay green unedited)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/ (task 011 golden baselines)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/DataverseUserClient.cs (read-only: IHttpContextAccessor L49/L72, context read L169, WhoAmI memo L226/L301)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/CallerWhoAmIMemo.cs (read-only)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/McpModule.cs (from 020: transport options)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/GetDecisionPlanTool.cs and CompleteDecisionTool.cs (from 023 and 024)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeProfileDispatcher.cs:88, 117-134 (existing detached-context workaround; context for the v1 limitation only)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">MCP host, McpModule transport options and McpTestHost</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">A10 auth on /mcp and the test authentication handler</dependency>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">spaarke_get_decision_plan (writes the plan-read stamp)</dependency>
      <dependency task="024" status="pending">spaarke_complete_decision (commit through DecisionCommitService)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">This task changes no file under src/. DataverseUserClient, CallerWhoAmIMemo, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerResolution, the decision services and every chat/AI path stay as they are (FR-10 option C). The PR shows git diff --stat limited to tests/ and projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The fail-closed tests prove three things: with no bearer token or no HttpContext, the real DataverseUserClient returns DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED); the fake wire handler records no Dataverse call; no app-only client is invoked (FR-10, ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No test asserts on, prints or logs a real bearer token or claim value. Tokens in fixtures are opaque test strings, and the test authentication handler exists only under tests/.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">T170 keeps WhoAmIs == 1 for REST, and the new MCP variant asserts WhoAmIs == 1 per spaarke_complete_decision commit. No existing test file is edited (FAILURE-MODES AP-9).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The PR is reviewed by unified-access-control-r2 and gets two adversarial-reviewer passes (root CLAUDE.md §8.5, auth tag).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;. The wire fake is a hand-written HttpMessageHandler subclass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any defect found and not fixed in this task is filed with /project-defer-issue-tracking (notes/defer-issues.md AND a GitHub issue), never one without the other (project CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run `bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master` (blocking Tier 1 'Format (changed C# files)'; it covers the new test files under tests/). CS0618 (obsolete API) is a build error since master 9456083c78: migrate the call or escalate, never suppress it in Directory.Build.props, NoWarn or a file-wide pragma.</constraint>
  </constraints>

